The portable C in the scenario setup-config: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-config.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 7, 14 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Execute options, which were Memory
allocation, Quick execute commands and TSR manager: the Keyboard options stand
five rows further up, at the top of the right half, with the last five rows of
the right half empty. Below the last box of the left half is Alt alone selects
menu, which is unticked there, and the three steps that untick Memory
allocation, tick Quick execute commands and untick TSR manager are left out;
Left from Clear keyboard buffer is Full screen, the box of its row, where it
was Show logical drive B:. The setup file that is saved has the three bytes of
those settings as it had them, 1, 0 and 1, where the original's has 0, 1 and 0
for the boxes unticked and ticked, and so another sum: the file differs in
those four bytes. The mouse pointer exchanges the colours of the cell that it
is on, the middle of the screen where nothing has moved it: the lines have
moved under it, and it stays

